---
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use Unity Test Framework.

- Prefer Edit Mode tests for pure gameplay and simulation logic.

- Use Play Mode tests only when behavior requires actual Unity GameObjects,
  Components, physics, navigation, scene lifecycle, or frame execution.

- Do not force MonoBehaviours into unit-testable abstractions purely for test coverage.
  Prioritize tests around deterministic domain rules and state transitions.
